/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/repairs.json" "file_sha256" "0328005daa91919dd8bb81fd729228440954ec812e808e91c99da77efc57aee9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653} {"question" "q-31272" "field" "answer" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "local_authored" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/repairs.json" "file_sha256" "0328005daa91919dd8bb81fd729228440954ec812e808e91c99da77efc57aee9" "transaction" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/transaction.edn" "transaction_sha256" "571ee7e4f8997fdfae74f800edd84d0efce760607b5043aa85a8d9d81962095f" "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/history-question-import-2026-10-04/format-audit/database-repair/verification.json" "basis" 653} {"question" "q-114250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "${lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)}{{x}^{2}-2x+1}=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "If we plug in $x=1$ we get the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0},$ so  we apply L'Hopital's rule to find the limit:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{[2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)]^{′}}{[{x}^{2}-2x+1]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{-2\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}{2x-2} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}{x-1}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThis time, the resulting limit still gives the indeterminate form $\\frac{0}{0}.$ To find the limit, we apply L'Hopital's rule once again. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{2+2\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)}{{x}^{2}-2x+1} & =-{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)}{x-1} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{[\\pi \\operatorname{sin}⁡(\\pi x)]^{′}}{[x-1]^{′}} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to 1}\\frac{{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(\\pi x)}{1} \\\\  & =-{\\pi }^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\pi  \\\\  & ={\\pi }^{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114250" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f338d77ee01746b9a0b348615cc7f4946f6911bf5686ee5f3f9adbf5eeafa1c3" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114250" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json"