loper/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114250" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\pi }^{2}"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-114250" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "{\\pi }^{2}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate the following limit:\n\n${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})}=$\n{{field-1}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)=-\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})=-\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{-\\infty }{-\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{(\\frac{3}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{3{x}^{-1}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f338d77ee01746b9a0b348615cc7f4946f6911bf5686ee5f3f9adbf5eeafa1c3" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/state.json" "file_sha256" "a546006f34867d121c7e5670d5d3de2f8e7d622cd5e0ed87e29b672e0d99d644" "basis" 582 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13948006/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003623/state.json" "file_sha256" "a27908fcf7e3ee75ae6093cbf46463237bda3d3a1e4f9a015437115aba1b7499" "basis" 1090 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003623/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-115526" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Here the limits of the numerator and denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)=-\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{-\\infty }{\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)}{\\operatorname{cot}⁡x} & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)]}^{′}}{[\\operatorname{cot}⁡x]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})}{-{csc}^{2}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{(\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x})}{(\\frac{1}{{sin}^{2}⁡x})} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{cos}⁡x{sin}^{2}⁡x}{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x} \\\\  & =-{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{cos}⁡x\\operatorname{sin}⁡x \\\\  & =-\\operatorname{cos}⁡0\\operatorname{sin}⁡0 \\\\  & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14003623/state.json" "file_sha256" "a27908fcf7e3ee75ae6093cbf46463237bda3d3a1e4f9a015437115aba1b7499" "basis" 1090 "verifica