 denominator are ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)=-\\infty $ and ${lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})=-\\infty ,$ respectively, so we have the case $\\frac{-\\infty }{-\\infty }.$\n\nApplying L'Hopital's rule, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)}{\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})} & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5x)]^{′}}{[\\operatorname{ln}⁡({x}^{3})]^{′}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{(\\frac{1}{x})}{(\\frac{3}{x})} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{{x}^{-1}}{3{x}^{-1}} \\\\  & ={lim}_{x\\to {0}^{+}}\\frac{1}{3} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/state.json" "file_sha256" "eba99a830e7033b322eceba6d91f900c953b715de77ce127a84e5a961e57bae8"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "543a47ee29201caea3d4fe4078ab9f2433b6e634fd1408c35864fe779760c0f4"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/state.json" "file_sha256" "eba99a830e7033b322eceba6d91f900c953b715de77ce127a84e5a961e57bae8"} {"question" "q-336758" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14068434/state.json" "file_sha256" "eba99a830e7033b322eceba6d91f900c953b715de77ce127a84e5a961e57bae8"}] "usage" {"q-115526" [] "q-114250" [] "q-31272" [] "q-336758"